==German==
===Etymology===
From an older word ''[[lass#German|lass, laß]]'' "languid, slothful, idle, weary" from {{etyl|goh}} {{term|laz|laz|slow, sluggish|lang=de}} from {{proto|Germanic|latas, lataz|slow, weary|lang=de}} from {{proto|Indo-European|lad-|slow, weary|lang=de}}. Akin to {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|læt|læt|slow, slack, lax, late|lang=ang}} ({{en}} ''[[late]]''), {{etyl|got|-}} {{term|𐌻𐌰𐍄𐍃|tr=lats||sluggish, weary|lang=got}}, {{etyl|la|-}} ''[[lassus]]'' "tired". More at [[late]].

